EXT. CIVIC PLAZA - CLIMATE MARCH - DAY

A river of cardboard signs. Drums. A bullhorn SQUEALS and dies.

RENA (V.O.)
Three thousand people, one bank across the square, and nobody looking at the loading dock. That's the whole trick. Be loud somewhere else.

RENA (30s, green vest, laminated MARSHAL badge) walks against the crowd, while BEA (20s, same vest, clipboard) cuts through the PROTESTERS ahead of her, a backpack riding high on her shoulders, and above them both a banner reading THERE IS NO PLANET B snaps in the wind as a helicopter's rotor THUMPS somewhere over the glass towers.

PROTESTERS
(chanting)
Pay for it! Pay for it! Pay for it!

Rena catches up. Bea doesn't slow.

RENA
You're early.

BEA
You're late. She said two-ten.

RENA
She said two-fifteen.

BEA
She said whatever gets us paid.

A cardboard polar bear bobs between them. Bea ducks it. Rena doesn't.

RENA (V.O.)
Bea never trusted a plan she didn't write. Which was fair. She wrote this one.

A whistle SHRIEKS. Police on bikes line the east side of the plaza. Bea steers Rena by the elbow toward the alley behind the bank.

BEA
Badge.

RENA
On.

BEA
Truck?

RENA
Ten minutes out. She's driving.

Bea stops short. Stares at her.

BEA
She's driving? She said she'd be here.

RENA
She's here. I mean she's close. She's in the truck. Bea, she's fine.

PROTESTERS
(chanting, louder)
Pay for it! Pay for it!

A speaker on the stage starts a speech. The crowd ROARS. Bea uses the noise and cracks the service gate with a bolt cutter. The lock CLANKS onto the pavement.

BEA
Then she's late and she's here. Pick one.

RENA (V.O.)
Forty seconds to the dock. Four minutes inside. Everybody on that square would remember the speech and nobody the van.

They slip through. The gate CLANGS shut behind them. The chanting drops to a muffled pulse.

INT. BANK - LOADING DOCK - CONTINUOUS

Concrete. Cold. A single camera in the corner, its red light blinking.

Rena looks up at it. Bea is already holding the backpack open.

BEA
Don't look at it.

RENA
I'm not looking at it.

BEA
You're looking at it.

Rena turns away. Beyond the wall, faintly, the crowd keeps chanting. Pay for it. Pay for it.
